{
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "$schema": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/sarif-2.1/schema/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "fullName": "Trivy Vulnerability Scanner",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/aquasecurity/trivy",
          "name": "Trivy",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "git2 has potential undefined behavior when dereferencing Buf struct "
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "If the Buf struct is dereferenced immediately after calling new() or default() on the Buf struct, a null pointer is passed to the unsafe function slice::from_raw_parts. According to the safety section documentation of the function, data must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. Thus, passing a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior."
              },
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h\nSeverity: LOW\nPackage: git2\nFixed Version: 0.20.4\nLink: [GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h)\nIf the Buf struct is dereferenced immediately after calling new() or default() on the Buf struct, a null pointer is passed to the unsafe function slice::from_raw_parts. According to the safety section documentation of the function, data must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. Thus, passing a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior.",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h**\n| Severity | Package | Fixed Version | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|LOW|git2|0.20.4|[GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h](https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-j39j-6gw9-jw6h)|\n\nIf the Buf struct is dereferenced immediately after calling new() or default() on the Buf struct, a null pointer is passed to the unsafe function slice::from_raw_parts. According to the safety section documentation of the function, data must be non-null and aligned even for zero-length slices or slices of ZSTs. Thus, passing a null pointer will lead to undefined behavior."
              },
              "properties": {
                "cvssv40_baseScore": 2.7,
                "cvssv40_vector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:L/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N/E:U",
                "precision": "very-high",
                "security-severity": "2.0",
                "tags": [
                  "vulnerability",
                  "security",
                  "LOW"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "version": "0.71.2"
        }
      },
